.\" The .TH version and date are placeholders, filled in by the packaging
.\" (scripts/dist.sh, ppa/debian/rules) from the release tag and its commit date.
.TH NODE\-TRACKER 1 "@DATE@" "node-tracker @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
node\-tracker \- alert when a Bitcoin node falls behind the chain tip
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B node\-tracker
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B node\-tracker
compares a Bitcoin node's block height with independent views of the chain
tip (Esplora servers such as \%mempool.space and \%blockstream.info, or other
bitcoind nodes) and with the node's own header height.
When the node falls more than a threshold behind, cannot be reached, or no
reference answers, it sends a Telegram message, and another one when the
node is back in sync.
Changes are debounced, and undelivered alerts are kept and retried.
.PP
Only the read\-only
.B getblockchaininfo
RPC is called.
Secrets (RPC password, bot token) are read from files or environment
variables, never from the configuration file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactive wizard for a first setup: finds the local bitcoind or asks for
the node, the references, the alert preset and the Telegram bot, tests
each answer, writes the configuration and its secret files, runs
.B check
and offers
.BR install\-service ;
see
.B SETUP OPTIONS
below.
.TP
.B run
Run as a daemon: one tick right away, then one every
.BR interval .
State and pending alerts are saved after each tick.
.TP
.B once
Run one tick and exit; for cron or a systemd timer.
Uses the same state file as
.BR run .
.TP
.B check
Dry run: sample every target and print a table, with a hint at the likely
cause of each error, then a verdict on the setup that lists the config
warnings.
No state is read or written and no alert is sent.
.TP
.B report
Send a status report of every target to every notifier, whatever the state.
.TP
.BR test\-notify " [\fIname\fR]"
Send a test message to the notifier
.IR name ,
or to all notifiers.
A failure is printed with a hint at its likely cause.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, commit, build time and Go version.
.TP
.B install\-service
Write and enable the systemd unit that runs this binary, then start it;
see
.B INSTALL\-SERVICE OPTIONS
below.
The configuration is validated first, and a changed unit or configuration
is only replaced with
.BR \-force .
.TP
.B help
Print a short usage message.
.SH OPTIONS
Flags follow the command, e.g.
.BR "node\-tracker once \-log\-level debug" .
.B node\-tracker
.I command
.B \-h
lists the flags of a command.
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Configuration file.
Default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/node\-tracker/config.yaml ,
that is
.I ~/.config/node\-tracker/config.yaml
unless
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set.
.TP
.BI \-state " file"
State file, for
.B run
and
.B once
only.
Default: the configuration's
.BR state_file ,
else
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/node\-tracker/state.json ,
that is
.IR ~/.local/state/node\-tracker/state.json .
.TP
.BI \-log\-format " format"
.B text
(default) or
.BR json .
Logs go to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-log\-level " level"
.BR debug ,
.B info
(default),
.B warn
or
.BR error .
.SH SETUP OPTIONS
Without
.BR \-non\-interactive ,
.B setup
asks its questions on the terminal; it refuses to run if standard input is
not a terminal.
Secrets are read with the echo off and never printed.
As a user, it writes
.I ~/.config/node\-tracker/config.yaml
(or the
.B \-config
file) with
.I telegram\-token
and, for an RPC user,
.IR <name>\-rpc\-password
next to it, all mode 0600; as root,
.I /etc/node\-tracker
(mode 0750, files 0640, group
.BR node\-tracker ),
as
.B install\-service \-system
expects.
A file that exists and differs is replaced only after a confirmation (or
with
.BR \-force ),
and kept as
.IR .bak .
.PP
For an RPC user it first asks whether the user and password exist already,
as on a node box (Umbrel, myNode, RaspiBlitz, StartOS).
If not, it can generate the RPC password and print the
.B rpcauth=
line for the node's
.IR bitcoin.conf ;
for a node elsewhere that defaults to no.
The chat id is found from a
.B /start
link with a one\-time code that the user opens in Telegram.
If Telegram does not answer, it offers to retry, to keep the token
untested and type the chat id, or to try through Tor
.RB ( socks5://127.0.0.1:9050 ),
which then goes into the configuration as the notifier's
.BR proxy .
.PP
The other flags are the answers of
.BR \-non\-interactive ,
for scripts and containers:
.TP
.B \-non\-interactive
Ask nothing: take the answers from the flags.
The node and the references are tested, and a test message is sent, but
only a token that Telegram rejects stops it.
.TP
.BI \-name " name"
Target name in alerts.
Default: the host name for a local node, else
.BR node .
.TP
.BI \-node\-url " url"
bitcoind RPC URL.
Default: the detected local bitcoind, with its cookie.
.TP
.BI \-cookie\-file " file"
bitcoind's
.IR .cookie .
.TP
.BI \-rpc\-user " user"
RPC username, instead of the cookie; needs
.BR \-rpc\-password\-file .
.TP
.BI \-rpc\-password\-file " file"
File holding the password of
.BR \-rpc\-user ;
it is copied next to the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-proxy " url"
Proxy for the node, e.g.
.BR socks5://127.0.0.1:9150 .
Default: from the environment; for .onion,
.BR socks5://127.0.0.1:9050 .
It is written to the configuration unless it is that default, as the
service may not have this shell's proxy variables.
.TP
.B \-allow\-insecure
Allow plain http to a node that is neither loopback nor .onion, e.g. on a
trusted LAN.
.TP
.BI \-references " urls"
Esplora API URLs, comma\-separated, or
.BR none .
Default: the public ones of the node's chain.
.TP
.BI \-preset " preset"
Alert preset:
.BR fast ,
.B balanced
(default) or
.BR quiet .
.TP
.BI \-token\-file " file"
File holding the Telegram bot token (required); it is copied next to the
configuration.
.TP
.BI \-chat\-id " id"
Telegram chat id or
.BI @ channel
(required).
.TP
.BI \-telegram\-proxy " url"
Proxy for Telegram, e.g.
.BR socks5://127.0.0.1:9050 ,
written to the configuration as the notifier's
.BR proxy .
Default: from the environment.
.TP
.B \-install\-service
Run
.B install\-service
at the end:
.B \-user
as a user,
.B \-system
as root.
On macOS, use
.B brew services start node\-tracker
instead.
.TP
.B \-force
Replace files that exist and differ, keeping the old config as
.IR .bak ;
old secret files are not kept.
.SH INSTALL\-SERVICE OPTIONS
Exactly one of
.B \-user
and
.B \-system
is required.
.TP
.B \-user
User service in
.IR ~/.config/systemd/user ;
no root needed.
Lingering is enabled, so the service keeps running after logout.
.B \-config
names the configuration the unit uses.
.TP
.B \-system
System service in
.IR /etc/systemd/system ,
run as the
.B node\-tracker
user, which is created if missing; needs root.
.B \-config
names the configuration to install as
.I /etc/node\-tracker/config.yaml
(mode 0640, group
.BR node\-tracker );
without it, the one already there is used.
Its secret files must already be in
.IR /etc/node\-tracker .
The binary and every directory above it must be owned by root and not
group\- or world\-writable, and every
.B cookie_file
must be readable by the service.
If the deb or rpm package's units already run this binary, they are
enabled instead.
.TP
.B \-timer
Install
.B node\-tracker\-once.timer
(one tick every 30 seconds) instead of the daemon.
.TP
.B \-dry\-run
Print the files and commands, change nothing.
.TP
.B \-force
Replace a changed unit or configuration, keeping the old one as
.IR .bak .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; every target is in sync.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, e.g. the state file could not be read or written, an alert is
still undelivered after
.BR once ,
or the run was interrupted.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Another node\-tracker holds the lock on the state file
.RB ( run
or
.BR once );
this run did nothing.
.TP
.B 4
A target was observed out of sync
.RB ( once ,
.BR check ,
.BR report ).
This is the monitored state, not a failure: alerts follow the debounced
state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR HTTP_PROXY ", " HTTPS_PROXY ", " NO_PROXY
Proxies for HTTP requests;
.B socks5://
works, e.g. for Tor.
See the configuration reference for per\-endpoint and per\-notifier proxies and .onion nodes.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directories of the default configuration and state files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/node\-tracker/config.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/node\-tracker/state.json
Default state file: target states and undelivered alerts.
It is locked through
.IR state.json.lock .
.TP
.IR /etc/node\-tracker/config.yaml ", " /var/lib/node\-tracker/state.json
Configuration and state of the systemd system service.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGINT
and
.B SIGTERM
stop
.B run
and
.BR once .
A tick interrupted while sampling leaves the state unchanged; alerts not
yet delivered stay queued in the state file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up, interactively:
.PP
.RS
.EX
node\-tracker setup
sudo node\-tracker setup    # the system service
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set up from a script:
.PP
.RS
.EX
node\-tracker setup \-non\-interactive \-token\-file token \-chat\-id 123456789 \-install\-service
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check that every node, reference and notifier is reachable:
.PP
.RS
.EX
node\-tracker check
node\-tracker test\-notify
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run one tick every minute from cron:
.PP
.RS
.EX
* * * * *  node\-tracker once 2>&1 | logger \-t node\-tracker
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The configuration reference, operations guide and design notes in
.IR /usr/share/doc/node\-tracker/docs/ ,
or at
.UR https://github.com/al\-maisan/node\-tracker
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/al\-maisan/node\-tracker/issues
.UE ;
security problems privately, see SECURITY.md.
